    "id": "pw8-arp-pluck",
    "name": "ARP PLUCK",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "A bright, short saw pluck (Filter 1 lowpass shapes the tone) driven by the arpeggiator: Up mode, tempo-synced to 1/16 notes, spanning 2 octaves, latch on so holding a chord briefly keeps it cycling. The 8-step pattern isn't uniform -- step 3 is accented, step 5 ratchets into a double-hit, and step 6 is a deliberate rest -- demonstrating per-step modifiers layered on top of the note sequence, not just a plain up-arp.",
